# HostingOS release signing keys — minisign (Ed25519) PUBLIC keys.
#
# Every release manifest and artefact must carry a minisign signature made
# by one of the keys below (or by a key that a manifest signed with one of
# them announced in `next_keys`, see docs/UPDATES.md "Key rotation").
#
# Format: one key per line, the base64 public key (the second line of a
# `minisign.pub` file, 56 characters starting with "RW"), optionally followed
# by whitespace and a label. Lines starting with `#` and blank lines are
# ignored. The build fails on a malformed line.
#
# This file is compiled into the binary (crates/hos-update/build.rs).
#
# It is EMPTY on purpose: no signing key has been generated yet. With no key,
# HostingOS still checks for and announces new releases (marked "unverified")
# but refuses to install them. To enable installs, generate a key pair as
# described in docs/RELEASING.md and add the public key here. Never commit
# the secret key.
